s case I  can make some videos out of it which is  great for everyone but by now these  videos often get more views than the  actual final videos of these projects so  I might as well focus on these videos as  their own thing and not just a byproduct  of some end product that I'm working  toward so maybe I'll think about those  kind of building ways a little bit more  in the future  but for these bridges it was honestly  kind of difficult because they're kind  of large kind of all over the place  and really I have to pay attention to  the most my new details to try and cover  up all of these little steel parts and  things that I want to make invisible as  much as possible so yeah that was  actually offered the catwalks and that  whole area over there but then I  realized there was still this bridge  which was so far kind of floating and  one of the problems that I had with this  bridge honestly is that it seemed  unsupportable because the way that it's  built is really giving myself a hard  time it was kind of stupid to do this in  the first place because you'll notice  that all of the other bridges they have  unbanked track and the track doesn't  move up or down maybe there's a slight  angle in the bridge or it's quite steep  actually but there's no difference in  steepness in most of the other bridges  but this one is just kind of annoying  because it goes from going up to going  down  was a bit of an arch in it and it also  goes from banking to the left to banking  to the right so it's really got damn  annoying bridge to support and that's  why I kind of didn't want to do it for  the longest time but at this point I  really figured you know I need to stop  procrastinating I didn't want to end the  episode at 14 minutes something so I  decided to build this thing as well and  add something to this surrounding area  and in the end what actually kind of  helped was to just build the wooden  planks according to the to the curvature  of the track I suppose try to just make  sure that they all connect to all of the  track pieces and then just kind of go  from there which didn't even turn out to  be that hard I just copy the curve from  one side over to the other and even if  the whole thing looks a little bit  strange I think this is just about the  only thing that I could do and at least  by combining all of these planks  together  it is a strangely curved bridge that  could theoretically actually be built in  real life as well so that's a problem  out of the way and I believe also that  with this bridge built all of the  bridges in the park are finished and  there's not much to worry about anymore  when it comes to that wrong with that no  I think that's it  there's just a lot of foliage and a lot  of work work to still do so I'm also  trying to chip away at the foliage and  rock work in every episode that I can as  well now here's a little bit of fun  detailing which I already did with some  of the lampposts and some my earlier  stuff but I don't do all the time  because it's something which takes way  too many faces and way too many time for  how much of a detail it really is but I  thought for this bridge you can actually  kind of work out and that's adding nails  to all of the logs so yeah it's not  something that you notice too much but  it definitely you know when you look at  the whole thing as a whole it even if  it's tan it doesn't stand out it makes  the bridge look a little bit more  realistic and I could insert the nails  here so I figured I might as well now  the final bit here is me trying to do  the foliage in such a way that I can  cover up what's backstage because  honestly the end of the park or at least  the end of the the  public part of the park and the border  between the park and the backstage areas  is just a few meters away from the path  here and I do wanna cover that up but at  the same time I do wanna make sure that  these these two drops are still open for  the view as much as possible so there's  a little bit of a transition from low  foliage to very tall foliage and some  other final details like the lamppost  over there  all of the lampposts on the catwalk  itself I honestly haven't checked at  nighttime yet and I'm definitely gonna  have to line up these bridges a little  bit more than they currently are but I  am pretty confident that these bridges  will look pretty swell at night and I  think these lamps do add a bit more of a  mind train touch to the right again  especially because there are these  really small oil lamps which I suppose  you could either just place on crates or  uses some kind of clutter or something  like that but I actually really like  putting these things on small posts  because they're one of the smaller cuter  lamp designs in the game and it just  looks quite simple and that's more or  less the look I'm going for here and the  final parts of this video should be  making this little jump from one walk to  the other most of this little unlike the  other one is supported by the  terraforming and it's really just  covering the ground at all points but  this is little space where it goes down  a bit which is partly because there's  the curve right underneath there and I  didn't want to make too much of a steep  steep cliff face because I felt like  that would look really unnatural like  there is no way that a natural mountain  terrain would be perfectly 45 degrees  and perfectly support this whole catwalk  so I wanted to make that a little bit  more random and at the same time it gave  me the opportunity to work on these  small terrain rail supports looking  things I honestly have no idea what to  call these things but sometimes when you  have a train rail that's built a few  meters of the ground you have these very  typical wooden support beams underneath  it so that's really what these things  are here for I think it adds a bit more  to the atmosphere and that's basically  it for this video so thank you guys for  watching I hope you guys enjoyed this  video as much as I did and I'll see you  next time  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

